WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Amy Adams.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before we move on, I have read
that you pick up hobbies

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
and maybe drop them
fairly quickly?

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.009 size:75% position:38%
This was a time that
a lot of people were

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:09.809 line:92%
at least trying new things

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you --
Was there anything that stuck?

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, but I did pick up
a lot of hobbies.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:17.884 size:84% position:42% line:92%
They just didn't stick.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a big fan of
string instruments, apparently

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
I tried the ukulele,
the mandolin.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.026
My husband got me this beautiful
cello for Christmas

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a couple years ago.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:27.894 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Can't play the cello.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Still haven't tried to
play the cello.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.699 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I did try the ukulele.

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
I tried to learn "Party Favor"
by Billie Eilish.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:36.136 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh?

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And my daughter was like,
"Yeah, you can't --

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not allowed to sing
Billie Eilish."

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say, the order seems t
be ukulele first,

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
not cello first.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
That seems like an
incredibly ambitious present

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.180 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to buy somebody.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I love the
sound of the cello,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:52.485 size:81% position:41%
and I think, you know,
he was being kind in

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:57.190
supporting my love of string
instruments that I can't play.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that definitely sound
like something you return

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're like, "Do you have,
like, CDs were people

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
play cello
that I could just put on?"

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The funny thing is,
I still believe

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to learn
all of this, Seth.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
I still really believe tha
I'm going to be

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:12.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
proficient at
string instruments.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know why.
-I like that.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we need more sort of
self-belief like that,

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.945 size:75% position:38%
so I'm going to jump
on board, as well.

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
And let's set a time.
-Okay.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:22.415 line:92%
Let's say three years from now

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.717 size:84% position:42%
you'll come on the show
and do cello for us.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:28.021
-Okay. I can play like seven
chords on the guitar right now

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, hopefully,
maybe I'll just learn

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.724 line:92%
those seven notes on the cello

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can come up
with a song or something.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.594 line:92%
-That sounds like a plan.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.530
Hey, so, "Hillbilly Elegy"
is this book by J.D. Vance

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's sort of his
personal history.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:42.569 size:88% position:44%
And he was involved in
the making of this film,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as was his mother.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does it have --
I imagine it must have

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:49.642 line:92%
an extra sense of responsibility

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:53.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you play a real perso
who's also nearby.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:54.781 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:58.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
She came to set
a couple of times,

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:00.987
luckily through some of th
scenes that weren't as heavy

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.922 size:75% position:38%
That would have been
really hard to film.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:05.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do -- I have a really
huge sense of responsibility

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
in playing somebody
that's out there

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I know she's going to
be watching this.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she was
incredibly courageous

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:15.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she's doing really well,
so that helps.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.302 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But it's intimidating.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:20.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, like --
Yeah, everything about it.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:21.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, coming up with
the look, the --

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.977
She was going through a really
hard time, too, in the film,

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:27.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, again, I'm just really
grateful for her participation

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you got to co-star
with Glenn Close.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:34.087
And there's obviously a lot of
hair and makeup and wardrobe

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.422
in this film that makes you both
look very different

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
from how we're used to
seeing you.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
But at the end of the film
it shows, I mean,

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.694 size:88% position:44%
the wardrobe department,
the makeup department,

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
the hair department
did an incredible job.

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.565 line:92%
You guys really hit the target

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:46.099 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:49.469
Glenn -- when you see
the picture of Glenn and Mawmaw,

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:50.570 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it is uncanny.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.240
They look so similar, and
their mannerisms and everything.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
She just nailed it.
She's amazing.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.279 size:88% position:44%
I loved working with her
and getting to know her.

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:00.246 size:88% position:44% line:92%
She's a wonderful woman.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:04.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have not -- It was --
I moved from a few years ago

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.619
and it was heartbreaking,
because I used to live

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the same apartment building
in New York as Glenn Close

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.424 line:92%
And seeing Glenn on the elevator

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:14.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
was just
the jackpot of jackpots.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you know her
particularly well

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
before you started
doing the film?

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.299 line:92%
-I didn't know her very well

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:22.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're really lucky
because we got to stay

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:25.438
in this bed-and-breakfast
when we were shooting in

00:03:25.438 --> 00:03:26.239 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Clayton, Georgia.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.073 line:92%
I have the mug from it here,

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I've been drinking
water from.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:31.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's, like, my favorite mug.
-That's a beautiful mug.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Yeah, I think so, too.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:35.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's from the
Beechwood bed-and-breakfast.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a -- And then there's
like, a wine --

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:38.451 line:92%
They have wine there, too.

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:44.090
So we would sit with the win
and have coffee and, you know...

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Very natural.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:45.825 size:88% position:44%
You can tell, by the way
you're drinking from it,

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's not your first sip
of anything from it.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.099
-This is why I was never good at
commercials, Seth.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:56.769
It's like, there's things
we're just not good at.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm bad with props.
-Yeah. It's true.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:01.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, especially in
a commercial --

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:04.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
In my early days, I had
a few commercial auditions

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when they put
a prop in the mix --

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm not
a good actor to begin with

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.816 size:81% position:41%
but it really, like,
cut my talent in half.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:10.483 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Oh, I'm bad with props.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every time they're like, "Okay
so, you're going to walk i

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.953
and you're gonna drop off your
purse and you're gonna dump it,"

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:14.554 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm like, "Ooh!

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:17.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay. How much time
do we have today?"

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you like --
Because I think some actor

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:22.328
really like to eat in scenes
because I think that takes the

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
out of their head.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.665 line:92%
Are you a good eating actor?

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:26.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Horrible.
-Really?

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know if I
just have a dry mouth,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I just always end up
with, like --

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:32.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't get the,
like, food ratio,

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:35.275
and it always ends up gettin
in the way of the dialogue

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:38.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I always --
I'm just really bad at it.

00:04:38.111 --> 00:04:40.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've seen people
who are really good eaters

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:40.980 line:92%
I've worked with a couple.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.417
-Yeah, I feel like Brad Pitt
could do, like, a "TED Talk" o

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
how to eat and act
at the same time --

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.121
or, like, one of those, like
"American Masters" series,

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:51.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think anybody --
I would watch that.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know how
they teach, like, stagecraft

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:55.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you learn how to
fight onstage or --

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:55.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:55.895 --> 00:04:57.964 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, that would be
a really important one,

00:04:57.964 --> 00:04:58.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think, that I --

00:04:58.598 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, because, like,
when Brad Pitt's eating, like,

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:03.236
a sandwich in a scene,
you're just never worried

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:05.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he's going to
spit lettuce on anybody.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just -- He seems very i
control of it.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If I'm eating,
you're just sure.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, "I'm not sure
where this ends up,

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.579 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but it's not good."

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will say,
I've seen films with you

00:05:15.415 --> 00:05:18.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you start to eat,
I just turn it off.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Films I'm enjoying.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm trying to think if
there's films.

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:22.522 line:92%
"Julie &amp; Julia," she eats a lot.

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:27.060
The Christmas scene -- I was
a master eater in that, so..

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.161 line:92%
-That's a lot of pressure.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, once again, like,
this proves

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you can play
a stringed instrument,

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you could get through
a whole film

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.101 line:92%
where you had to eat that much

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:38.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If I could just
put my mind to it, yeah.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is always so lovely
to see you.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.176
I wish you and your family
a very happy Thanksgiving,

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:45.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thanks, as always,
for making time for us, Amy.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.880 line:92%
-Thanks. You as well. Be well.

